-- 0209_a_catalog_worth_the_name
--
-- 2,931 Gu arrived as a wiki dump. 35 were already in the game. This adds the
-- other 2,834 and shuts the door on the top four ranks.
--
-- WHAT WAS THROWN AWAY. 18 rows are wiki furniture that the scrape swept up
-- with the rest - Template:, User:, "Page List/Gu", "Policies and Guidelines",
-- "Editing Playground", and two rows named nothing but "Gu". 46 more are the
-- same Gu listed twice under two ranks with identical Path, power and role;
-- the first listing wins. 33 name a Gu the game already has.
--
-- THE 35 WIN. Where the dump and the game disagree about one of the original
-- 35 - the dump files Battle Bone Wheel at rank 3 and Golden Centipede at
-- rank 5, the game at 4 and 1 - the game is not moved. Those Gu are held by
-- players, priced by recipes, and placed in regions; a rank is not a spelling.
--
-- PATHS ARE NOT LABELS HERE, so eleven of the dump's do not become new ones.
-- A Path in this game carries a matchup chart, an attainment ladder, herbs, a
-- technique at every rank and a pill kind; inventing eleven more would leave
-- eleven Paths that lose every matchup and teach nothing. They fold instead,
-- onto the word this game already uses for the same thing:
--
--     dark -> shadow      snow -> ice           blade -> sword
--     weapon -> metal     pill -> refinement    emotion -> human
--     phantom -> illusion information -> wisdom sound -> wind
--     killing -> blood    chaos -> rule
--
-- chaos folds onto rule because the dump itself files Chaotic Intent Gu under
-- rule, and Law Unraveler is a Gu about laws either way.
--
-- THE 286 WITH NO PATH are read off their food instead: 284 eat `essence`,
-- which is primeval essence, which is the Qi path; 2 eat jade, which is Earth.
--
-- EFFECTS ARE TRANSLATED, NOT COPIED. The dump carries 2,643 distinct flavour
-- codes. 0036 was explicit that an effect is a word the combat code reads and
-- a ceiling it respects - 2,643 uncapped words would be 2,643 lies. Every Gu
-- is rewritten in the 32-word vocabulary that exists, by rule: what the dump
-- says it DOES wins, then its Path, then whether it attacks, defends, moves or
-- supports. A Gu whose own code says `plunder` lends Gathering Yield whatever
-- its Path; a Soul Gu that says nothing lends Suppression.
--
-- MAGNITUDES SIT INSIDE THE BAND THE 35 ALREADY OCCUPY. Each effect has a
-- rank 1 value taken from what the hand-tuned Gu already pay (attack power
-- 0.06, evasion 0.06, penetration 0.10), multiplied up the rank ladder and by
-- where the Gu's own power sits among its rank. No single Gu may take more
-- than three fifths of an effect's ceiling: the cap exists so a build is
-- assembled out of several Gu, not finished by one.
--
-- RANK 6 AND UP CANNOT DROP. That is the ask, and it is written as a rule
-- rather than as an absence: `gu_max_droppable_rank` is 5, `roll_gu_drop`
-- reads it, and `gu_region_drops` refuses a row above it - so the gate cannot
-- be walked around later by adding a drop row and forgetting why. Raising it
-- is one UPDATE. The 589 Gu above the line are in the catalogue, readable in
-- /gupedia, and found nowhere.
--
-- DIVINE HAD NO PRICE. `gu_refine_rarity_costs` carried eight of the nine
-- rarities; a Divine Gu would have had a recipe and no cost, and
-- `gu_recipe_costs` INNER JOINs that table - so it would have vanished from
-- /refine entirely rather than being expensive. It gets a multiplier between
-- mythic and unique.
--
-- Nothing anybody owns is touched.
--
-- Forward-only. Do not edit once applied.


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The gap and the gate
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

INSERT INTO gu_refine_rarity_costs (rarity, multiplier) VALUES ('divine', 11.00);

